  "Question": "The number \\(2.5252525\\ldots\\) can be written as a fraction. When reduced to lowest terms the sum of the numerator and denominator of this fraction is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(7\\)",
    "B": "\\(29\\)",
    "C": "\\(141\\)",
    "D": "\\(349\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The block \\(52\\) repeats every two decimal places, so multiplying by \\(100\\) aligns the repeating tail with itself. Let\n\\[\nx=2.525252\\ldots.\n\\]\nThen \\(100x=252.525252\\ldots\\). Subtracting the original equality cancels the complete repeating tails exactly:\n\\[\n100x-x=252.525252\\ldots-2.525252\\ldots=250.\n\\]\nHence \\(99x=250\\), giving \\(x=\\dfrac{250}{99}\\).\n\nSince \\(250=2\\cdot5^3\\) and \\(99=3^2\\cdot11\\) have no prime factors in common, this fraction is already in lowest terms. The requested sum is \\(250+99=\\boxed{349}\\), choice D.",
